  "title": "P17/P18 read and search economy, shadow: deterministic repeated-read and repeated-search detection in the Jev tool gate, evidence-pool awareness, action_gate decision rows, read-economy scorecard; nothing blocked",
  "spec": "Facts (Planner grep, provenance repo): orchestrator/jev_gate.py is the PreToolUse gate for Claude worker sessions (.claude/hooks/jev-gate.sh): it reads the transcript's recent tool calls (read_transcript, RECENT_LIMIT), keeps a session state with exact-repeat detection (_session_state, _record_call, _target_mtime, lines ~150-200), asks Jev needed/redundant/destructive on a deterministic sample ([jev] gate_mode sample/log/block, sample_rate) and logs every evaluated call to .orchestrator/runs/jev/gate.jsonl; [jev] block_repeats = false today; guardrails.sh is the only hook that blocks destructive commands. T-0774 declared the gate's Jev boundary (site \"gate\"). evidence.EvidencePool(goal) (T-0794) holds content-addressed evidence with commit freshness; T-0800 fills it from execute/review packet builds.\nDo:\n1. orchestrator/read_economy.py (new): pure functions over the gate's per-session call history: `classify(call, history, *, evidence=None, head_sha=None)` returns {\"kind\": one of \"first_read\", \"repeated_read_unchanged\" (same path, mtime and size unchanged since the earlier read), \"repeated_read_changed\", \"repeated_search\" (Grep/Glob with identical pattern+path+flags), \"narrower_search\" (same path, pattern contains the earlier pattern), \"evidence_available\" (a fresh source_chunk for that path exists in the EvidencePool for the task's goal at head_sha), \"other\"; \"tokens_estimate\": for reads the file size // 4 bounded by the tool's limit/offset when given, for searches the earlier result size when the transcript carries it else None; \"would_suppress\": True only for repeated_read_unchanged and repeated_search}. Never touches Jev.\n2. jev_gate.py: before the Jev sample decision, run read_economy.classify for Read/Grep/Glob calls and: log the classification into the gate.jsonl row (fields read_kind, tokens_estimate, would_suppress); record decision_log.record(kind=\"action_gate\", subject=task id, candidates=[\"allow\", \"suppress\"], hard_constraints=[\"guardrails.sh decides destructive\", \"block_repeats=false\"], deterministic={\"read_kind\", \"tokens_estimate\", \"would_suppress\"}, jev={\"needed_p\", \"redundant_p\"} when a Jev verdict exists, selected=\"allow\", reason=read_kind, mode=[jev].gate_mode) at most once per call and never for skipped/protected calls; behaviour stays fail-open and nothing is denied (block_repeats stays false; do not touch the block path). Only ambiguous kinds (\"repeated_read_changed\", \"narrower_search\", \"other\" with a prior call on the same path) count toward the Jev sample; first reads never consume Jev budget (document this as the P18 rule \"Jev only for ambiguous semantic equivalence\").\n3. Scorecard: `read_economy.summary(root)` over gate.jsonl: per role and per task_class: reads, repeated_read_unchanged, repeated_search, evidence_available, tokens_avoidable (sum of tokens_estimate where would_suppress), jev_calls_avoided (first reads not sampled), and the false-suppression proxy: a would_suppress read whose path was edited by the same session within the next 5 calls (needs the edit; if the transcript does not show later calls at gate time, compute it offline from the transcript path recorded in the row). `orchestrator scorecard --reads` prints it.\n4. Docs: docs/context-economy/09-read-economy.md (\u226460 lines): kinds, what shadow logs, the P18 rule, what active would do (suppress with a structured \"already read at <call>\" reply) and why it is not enabled (needs the false-suppression proxy at zero over min_samples), revert path.\nTests (unittest, `import _harness` first; the gate tests already exist in tests/test_jev_gate.py, extend them): tests/test_read_economy.py::test_repeated_read_unchanged_detected_by_mtime_and_size, ::test_repeated_search_and_narrower_search, ::test_evidence_available_from_pool, ::test_summary_counts_tokens_avoidable_and_false_suppression_proxy; tests/test_jev_gate.py::test_first_reads_skip_jev_sample_and_log_read_kind, ::test_gate_never_denies_on_would_suppress.\nDo not ask questions; decide and note decisions in the result. Never quote double-brace placeholder tokens literally.",
