    "summary": "Fix-round commit 43f6b76 addresses both round-1 comments: the block_repeats check (jev_gate.py:406) now runs before the economy 'not ambiguous' short-circuit (moved to jev_gate.py:414), so repeated identical Read/Grep/Glob calls are still blocked once block_repeats=true; the block path's _log call now passes economy=economy plus transcript_path/call_index/role/task_class, so read_kind, tokens_estimate, and would_suppress land in every classified gate.jsonl row including blocked ones. test_block_repeats_denies was reverted to use the default Read tool (the Bash workaround is gone), and the two new tests (test_block_repeats_still_reaches_block_path_with_economy, test_block_path_row_carries_economy_fields) correctly exercise both the unchanged-repeat block case (would_suppress=True) and the changed-content block case (would_suppress=False, tokens_estimate matches new file size) against read_economy.classify's actual semantics. No regressions found in the reasoning.",
